<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Wiki-Layer Ontology ~ the record

''The doctrine stands at'' <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/wiki-layer-ontology`>>: the Rosetta table, the quine, a bag by capability, the oracle planes, Laws 1-5 and 4b, the daemon wiki and the shore law. This carrier keeps the record beside it: the alpha transition (why the tree does not yet wear the shore), the crossing grain as settled, the transitive closure held open, the pack refinements owed, and what the build owes the oracle planes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/alpha-transition`>>

!! The Alpha Transition — why the tree does not wear the shore

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/wiki-layer-ontology#/shore-law`>> rules the working↔canon crossing and <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/wiki-layer-ontology#/quine`>> rules that ''no wiki writes into its own canon''. The tree enacts neither: the alpha practice edits canon carriers in place. A reader who meets `bags/` before this section reads the alpha practice as the law; this section names the gap.

!!! `bags/` holds the fresh-vessel seed

`bags/` holds the git-tracked carriers a fresh vessel seeds from, beside committed `genesis/` (`founding-runbook#/fresh-state`). No existing CRDT document needs to survive a re-found. Through the alpha, a hand edits carriers in place, re-stamps them and commits them (`canon-boundary#/the-promotion-boundary`). ''That names a property of an alpha in which no CRDT document needs to survive, never a property of `bags/`.'' Under the designed model the document persists and disk projects from it.

!!! Three roles ride `bags/`; exactly one retires

| role | what it does | standing |
|---|---|---|
| ''the hand-edit door'' | a hand saves into a canon carrier and the ingest gate carries it into the records | ''the alpha scaffold — THIS RETIRES'' |
| ''the genesis / cold-boot seed'' | a fresh vessel re-forges its whole substrate from these carriers | ''permanent'' |
| ''the canon of record'' | git-tracked carriers at hostless `lar:///` addresses | ''permanent'' |

''The retiring role names a DOOR, never mutability.'' `canon-boundary#/the-promotion-boundary` holds that an address stands while its bytes move, and that law survives the transition whole — canon carriers keep changing. What moves: a hand's save lands in the wiki's `@working` layer (`wikis/{slug}`) and reaches canon by the cap-gated promotion `MOVE`, rather than by typing into `bags/` and letting the ingest gate carry it down.

⚠ ''`residency` names two things and a reader meets both right here.'' The promotion rides CANON residency — the ACTION verb surface (`residency-model#action-verb-surface`). `lares wiki status` reports something else: a vessel's hot/cold cache standing (pinned · wela · anu). Two offices, one word, neither renaming; a reader takes the sense from the surrounding verb.

!!! The carriers already standing stay put

Every git-tracked `.mem` carrier in `bags/` sits at a hostless address, ''which names the completed END of a promotion rather than a violation of one'' — `canon-boundary#/the-promotion-boundary` reads a hostless address in a canon bag exactly that way. ''Nothing migrates.'' The corpus keeps its bytes, its addresses and its git history; the transition changes the door a future edit walks through, never where a standing carrier lives. No corpus witness sees a changed byte on account of this ruling.

!!! The window carries the risk, never the destination

The habit and the design disagree while the move runs, and ''every instrument sides with the habit'': the vessel grants literal disk mirrors on `bags/lares` and `bags/lararium`, the ingest gate weighs a disk read against the last-projected hash to decide noop / ingest / conflict (`synced-tree`), and the working surface uses the `wikis` mirror root beside `bags` under the same worker root. A weld that refuses hand edits to `bags/` therefore refuses the very work that carries the house across.

''ORDERING: the hand-edit weld lands LAST and stays silent throughout.'' The standing carriers keep their hand-edit door until the working surface stands and the promotion `MOVE` runs; arming that weld earlier stops the transition rather than guarding it.

!!! What ''disk-leaning'' means under the design

`disk-projection#/core-claim` grades `bags/` ''disk-leaning'' against `wikis/`'s ''store-leaning''. Two grounds sit under that one word, and only one of them retires:

* ''the authoring grain'' — a hand edits one whole carrier: one meme, one `.md`, one git history (`disk-projection#/granularity`, the co-projection ruling). ''This HOLDS.'' Merge authority routes through the CRDT under either model; the grain never moves.
* ''the surviving copy'' — disk outlasts each refounding, so disk answers first. ''This RETIRES'' with the disposable substrate.

So a reader takes the grading as a statement about ''grain'', never as a licence for a wiki to write its own canon.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/crossing-grain`>>

!! Crossing Grain — SETTLED (operator, 2026-06-10)

The wiki-level crossing earns a ''bag-grain verb pair'', SPARQL Update derived: `CREATE` mints the new coordinate (`CREATE GRAPH` analog), bag-grain `COPY` grants residency for every title with `change-id` preserved under one `transfer-id` family, and registration lands as a `holdings` accession in `@catalog` (the union catalog). Operator ruling: pono web3 models in place early — a first-class mint verb keeps registry, capability gates, and audit ledger aligned with the coordinate-space model before batch-conventions calcify. Routing rides the sovereign-worker rail (verb-tiddler → summons → outcome; admin island executes; orichalcum `admin` on destination + `edit` on `@catalog`). Full law: `residency-model#action-verb-surface`, bag-grain section. Implementation pending in `residency-actions.ts`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/open-transitive-closure`>>

!! Open — Transitive Closure (held, not settled)

When `@caverns-of-neo-thracia` mounts `elyncia`, does it inherit `elyncia`'s library list automatically, or does its recipe name the full flattened stack? Auto-transitive reads convenient yet imports diamond/version conflicts into cascade order; explicit-flattened reads verbose yet keeps every wiki's shadowing order operator-visible and deterministic. Current lean (Provisional): explicit-flattened with a mint-time helper that //suggests// the closure — convenience at registration, determinism at boot, in the spirit of a lockfile. The decision waits on live witness of real chains mounting.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/pack-refinements`>>

!! Pack Model — Owed Refinements (held; external precedent)

The multi-tiddler ''pack'' (hold-a-set) crossing rides the same //working ↔ canon// law: a member edit shadows UP into `@working`, the pack file stays one file on disk (projection SUPPRESSED for pack members by `isPackMember`), and a deliberate ''REPACK'' re-renders. ''Built'': the in-VM deserializer, `$:/`-aside provenance (`OriginalTiddlerPaths`), REPACK, and the projection-suppress loop-stopper. FOUR refinements stay owed, each read off external precedent (Git · OCI · Nix · Unison · matview · overlayfs):

* ''One descriptor·kind'' — the three //what-belongs// mechanisms (title-nesting · aside-JSON · plugin payload) collapse to ONE aside descriptor `{member content-DIGEST, kind, annotations}`, never an in-band member edit (OCI: layers[] vs subject = one shape, differ by relationship-kind).
* ''Filter-seed matview'' — `OriginalTiddlerPaths` stands as a materialized view with its definition thrown away. Store the filter-SEED beside the snapshot; REPACK = `REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW`; add a sync-audit (snapshot provably re-derivable FROM the seed, or the pair flags drift). full-REFRESH (REPACK) vs incremental-REFRESH (delta) = two verbs.
* ''COW-overlay PACK/UNPACK + atomic PROMOTE'' — LOWER (canon, read-only) + UPPER (`@working`) + WORK; copy-up-on-first-write CONSTITUTES UNPACK; overlay never destroys lower = //working shadows canon// in fs primitives. PACK = ONE atomic reconcile (shadow-paging root-swap) coalescing MOVE's two halves — the missing verb. VCS vocab NOT adopted (''rite not drift'').
* ''Agile algorithm-tagged digest'' — identity = `algorithm:hex` content digest, SRI strongest-wins (no flag-day), identity-hash SEPARATED from location/attestation (referrers OVER digests, the chain links digests never re-hashes locations).

Both #42 operator forks resolved by intervening work: `SHA256(uri+path)` retired (content-addressing reframe); the Confluence already stands as ONE gate over a semantic congruence `≈`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/owed`>>

!! Owed ~ what the build owes beside the doctrine, and the readings it replaced

!!! What the Kahu Plane road owes the floor (from api/pono/wiki-layer-ontology#/oracle-planes)

The Kahu Plane road owes the floor's frozen seed-derived address and no-writer rule.

!!! The public answer, as the build owes it (from api/pono/wiki-layer-ontology#/oracle-planes)

The WHO board address derives from the Nexus key. LAW THE BUILD OWES: one public answer per Nexus names the floor CID; that Nexus's Kahu steward signs it, and a herm carries and presents it without signing it. No tender name reaches a stranger; the steward seal carries the authority. The Kahu Plane owns the steward-signing shape, and R-WIRE owes answer carriage. The Kahu Plane road owes the floor's frozen seed-derived address and no-writer rule, the crossroads address derivation, and retirement of `CREATE --plane oracle`.

!!! The daemon's own canon (from api/pono/wiki-layer-ontology#/the-daemon-wiki)

The 2026-09-02 ruling read that `@daemon` "will likely seed a canon-bag layer of its own"; the face's local canon `bags/daemon-<F>` stands that layer (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/daemon-and-domain`>>).

!!! The face gate the vessel binding replaced (from api/pono/wiki-layer-ontology#/the-daemon-wiki)

''A wiki's instance slots once bound only where a FACE stood'' — so a Herm resolved none, and the daemon could not consume the resolver it supplies. That gate remained from Herm and Lararium standing as separate ''classes'' before they became one capability stack, and it read as structure while standing as residue.

<<~/ahu>>

